{
  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_027 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieves 0.4348 acc / 0.4234 F1, outperforming config_005 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) at 0.4106 acc / 0.3785 F1, indicating that adding image features with concat fusion is beneficial. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the fusion mechanism itself (concat vs. weighted) is a meaningful design choice, or whether the gain is purely from the additional modality. This experiment (config_051) is a clean single-variable change from config_027—only the fusion type shifts from concat to weighted—while holding RNA encoder (scgpt), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), profile setting (singleprofile), and aggregation (None) constant. If weighted fusion improves performance, it reveals that modality weighting matters and guides future multiprofile/aggregation experiments; if it does not, concat is confirmed as sufficient and we can redirect budget toward testing aggregation or profile settings. This is the most informative next step under a limited budget because it isolates one important design axis from the current best configuration with minimal confounding."
}

